;
NDSCAN - REFRESH NAMED DIRECTORIES

A - Refresh named directories

:A
REFRESH NAMED DIRECTORIES

    NDSCAN J:
    NDSCAN P:
    NDSCAN J: /Q

Rebuilds named directories for one drive by examining its user areas
0 through 15 for extensionless -NAME marker files. Areas without a
marker lose their old names. Other drives' directory names are retained.

MOUNT normally performs this operation automatically after a swap.
/Q suppresses the success message, but not errors.

Callers need read access to all sixteen user areas on the selected
drive. Duplicate names, conflicting markers, disk errors or a full
name table prevent the update. The previous names remain intact.

If a mount succeeds but its scan fails, the new disk is already in
place. Use numeric DUs until the scan succeeds or restore the default
volume. NDSCAN does not change files or grant access permissions.

See HELP MOUNT, HELP CPM and HELP DISKS.
